  "generated_text": "First, we perform the $45^\\circ$ rotation around the origin. A $45^\\circ$ rotation of a complex number $a + bi$ is equivalent to multiplying by $e^{i\\pi/4} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} + i\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$.\n\n\\[\n(-3 - 8i) \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} + i\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) = \\frac{-3}{\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{8i}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{-3 - 4i}{\\sqrt{2}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we perform the dilation centered at the origin with a scale factor of $\\sqrt{2}$. This dilation scales the complex number by $\\sqrt{2}$.\n\n\\[\n\\frac{-3 - 4i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\cdot \\sqrt{2} = \\frac{-3\\sqrt{2} - 4i\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}} = -3 - 4i\n\\]\n\nThus, the resulting complex number after both transformations is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3 - 4i}\n\\]",
